<title>USA: Showers, mild temps seen for Brazil coffee - WSC.</title>
<headline>Showers, mild temps seen for Brazil coffee - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A warm ridge of high pressure dominating Brazil's coffee belt is expected to continue for the next seven days, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies were observed throughout the region this morning. Temperatures remained near to above normal levels with lows ranging from 54-63 F (12-17 C).</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected to continue through today. There is a chance of scattered showers and thunderstorms develping on Thursday and Friday. Lows will continue to range from the middle 50's to middle 60's F (middle to upper teens C).</p>
<p>The extended outlook calls for scattered showers in all areas on Saturday and Sunday with temperatures remaining near to above normal. There is no damaging cold expected, according to WSC.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
